<header><p class="st-kicker">khanate · Indian princely states</p><h1 class="st-title">Khanate of Kalat</h1><p class="st-meta">1666 CE – 1955 CE (approx.) · capital Kalat</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The Brahui-led khanate of Balochistan, the paramount power of the region for nearly three centuries until merged into Pakistan.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>Around 1666 the Ahmadzai chief Mir Ahmad Khan I established a Brahui-led confederacy based at Kalat, in the highlands of central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/balochistan">Balochistan</a>, on the borderlands of Safavid <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/persia">Persia</a> and Mughal <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The Khan ruled through a tribal confederacy of Sarawan and Jhalawan chiefs. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nasir-khan-i-of-kalat">Mir Nasir Khan I</a>, who reigned for much of the late 18th century, organised the army and administration and extended rule to the coast. In 1839 British troops stormed Kalat and killed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mehrab-khan">Mehrab Khan</a>; later treaties made it a British-protected state, with <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kharan-state">Kharan State</a> and other chiefdoms as feudatories.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>Khan <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ahmad-yar-khan">Ahmad Yar Khan</a> declared independence in 1947 but acceded to <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/islamic-republic-of-pakistan">Pakistan</a> in March 1948. Kalat joined the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/baluchistan-states-union">Baluchistan States Union</a> and was absorbed into <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/west-pakistan">West Pakistan</a> in 1955.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/khanate-of-kalat.jpg" alt="Khanate of Kalat" width="320" height="213"><figcaption>Image: WikiCobalt-Chloride- · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:FlagofKalat.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1666 CE – 1955 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>khanate</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>tribal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Kalat</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Mir Ahmad Khan I, Mir Nasir Khan I, Ahmad Yar Khan</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Sunni Islam</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Brahui, Balochi</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/pakistan">Pakistan</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Kalat State, Kalat</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1810&amp;focus=khanate-of-kalat" aria-label="Khanate of Kalat on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="6418 1116 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Khanate of Kalat lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M6738 1372L6298 1144M6738 1372L6757 1183M6738 1372L7364 1601M6738 1372L7364 1602M6738 1372L6778 1519M6738 1372L6738 1372M6738 1372L6751 1470M6738 1372L6710 1388M6738 1372L6666 1478"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M6298 1144h0M6757 1183h0M7364 1601h0M7364 1602h0M6778 1519h0M6738 1372h0M6751 1470h0M6710 1388h0M6666 1478h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M6738 1372h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M6738 1372h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Kalat. <a href="/atlas?year=1810&amp;focus=khanate-of-kalat">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
